# Fixed defect 577, 2026-10-10 (panel 206 R1 and R4; the critic's `c03`): a
# group's constant has no body, so its value is C's, platform by platform, and
# the walk over a written body gives it none. `INT64_MAX + 1` is not judged
# when the program is compiled, and it aborts where `N` is read, as overflow
# aborts at every width (spec § 7), the `1` before it flushed first. Defect
# 579 is the build-time probe that would refuse it.

extern "stdint.h"
    constant INT64_MAX: i64

constant N: i64
    INT64_MAX + 1

function main()
    print(1)
    print(N)
